OL,3,GNEWSADogs at risk after toxin kills
OL,4,Abirds at Rye
OL,5,
OL,6,FA number of dead birds have been found
OL,7,Fat a reserve, Sussex Wildlife Trust has
OL,8,Fsaid.
OL,10,FThe birds at Rye Harbour Nature Reserve
OL,11,Fare thought to have been killed by
OL,12,Favian botulism, a disease caused by a
OL,13,Ftoxin that appears in warmer weather.
OL,15,F"Recent hot and dry conditions have
OL,16,Fcaused water levels to fall
OL,17,Fsignificantly, creating conditions in
OL,18,Fwhich the toxin can develop," said the
OL,19,Ftrust.
OL,23,APub: 21-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
